-- the reckoning --
  you came out the other side of it.
  floors: 5 of 5   turns: 25
  it was starting to notice you: resonance 2.
  with a little on your hands: corruption 4.
  3 people saw you coming. 2 of them are still alive.

  nurse        -> cleric   of fire   (soft to frost)
  MIG 3   FOC 5   GRI 3   WIT 4
  hp 18/39   mp 18/20   resonance 2   corruption 4

  THE HOLLOW THRONE   (sacred)
  it has been waiting the whole time, and it knew which way you would come.

-- an item is an art, and that is the whole of the design --
  a flask of oil    [ground_add]
  a waterskin       [ground_add]
  tinder            [ground_add]
  a censer          [ground_add]
  grit-salt         [ground_clear]
  smelling salts    [heal restore]
  a stone that hums [attune]
-- a chef comes down already carrying, and nobody else does --
  chef       ["a flask of oil", "a waterskin"]
  soldier    []
  librarian  []
-- four slots, and a fifth is refused by name --
  your hands are full -- put something down first (smelling salts)
  after putting one down, it fits: fax
-- POUR, THEN LIGHT: two rules that were always there, combined by a player --
  ember on its own:               2 done, 0 taken, asks nothing
  a flask of oil leaves the floor: sacred, damp, gas
  and then ember:                 5 done, 6 taken, asks ignition
  and pouring one onto a floor that is already gas:
     the floor is already gas
-- a chef's consumable does not end the turn; everybody else's does --
  chef   turn 1 -> 1
  nurse  turn 1 -> 2
-- and a flask previews exactly as it resolves --
  7 items, 0 that resolved differently the second time

-- what a turn does to the mountain --
  a fire art:                    heat +2
  a frost art:                   heat -1
  an earth art:                  wet -1
  a void art:                    foul +2
  a storm art:                   foul +1
  fire on a damp floor:          heat +2  wet +1
  frost on a damp floor:         heat -1  wet +1
  a turn that ended alight:      heat +1  foul +1
  grit-salt:                     foul -2
  a heal, on ordinary ground:    nothing
  and nothing leaves 0..10:      0, 10
-- and what it does to a room you walk into, on arrival and never otherwise --
  the wet stair, calm:           damp, dark
  the wet stair, heat 4:         dark, dry
  the wet stair, heat 7:         dark, dry, gas
  the iron gallery, wet 4:       metal, windy, damp
  the iron gallery, foul 4:      metal, windy, choking
  the frozen chapel, foul 4:     sacred, damp, choking
  the frozen chapel, foul 8:     damp, choking   (it is not sacred any more)
  heat 6 against wet 4:          dark, dry
  heat 4 against wet 6:          damp, dark
  heat 5 against wet 5:          damp, dark   (a tie condenses)
-- a fire on dry ground is a different animal --
  burning, ordinary ground:      3 to the room, and the floor is now: 
  burning on dry ground:         6 to the room, and the floor is now: burning, dry
  burning with gas still to eat: 3 to the room, and the floor is now: burning
  choking costs everything 2:    2 to the room, and the floor is now: choking

-- 22. a floor that meant something will not help somebody like you --
  clean, on sacred ground:       +11
  corruption 5, on sacred:       +5
  corruption 5, anywhere else:   +11
-- 23. and void gets cheaper, which is the whole point of the meter --
  hollow (3 will), clean:        0 net
  hollow (3 will), corruption 5: -1 net
-- 26. as does your own element, once the world minds you enough --
  flare at resonance 0:          4
  flare at resonance 8:          3
-- 24. a hollow place, which nothing can lay down but you --
  glimmer, ordinarily:           2
  glimmer, hollow:               1
  whisper, ordinarily:           2
  whisper, hollow:               3
  consecrate, hollow:            there is nothing here that will take that
-- 25. what your own element costs you, and when it stops --
  element     raw  mastered
  fire          3         0
  frost         2         0
  storm         5         0
  earth         3         0
  void          2         0
  light is absent, and that is the point: it costs its user nothing to
  begin with, so there is nothing for mastery of it to hand back.

-- THE ASSERTION THIS WHOLE THING EXISTS FOR --
   ignite the gas hall with a person standing in it, and then with a rat
   of exactly their size standing exactly where they stood.
  the rules did the same arithmetic, line for line: fax
     note       0
     damage     5
     damage    10
     kill       0
     ground     0
     hurt       6
  and the only difference is rule 27, which is the one rule about them:
     corruption 0 against 3
-- an untargeted strike never finds them --
  it hit: a boil of rats
-- a floor with a survivor on it still ends --
  standing: 1   cleared: fax   and they take no turn: fax
-- a Mend can be pointed at one of them --
  their hp 2 -> 6, marked tended, and yours untouched at 20
  untargeted it is still you: 31
-- and what became of them --
  killed  -> killed
  helped  -> helped
  left    -> left

